 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508255,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Choose the correct equation for the graph shown:\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2adda313dcbcdbed.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 5. The line passes through the points, (negative 8, 0) and (0, 4).\">\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 995748,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = 2x + 4\">y = 2x + 4</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 995749,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4\">y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4</span>",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 995750,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y =  - 2x + 4\">y =  - 2x + 4</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 995751,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4\">y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response",
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Test the points for all the options. Only the correct option works.</p>\n<p>Correct option: <span data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(0, 4)\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4 = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( 0 \\right) + 4\"></span></p>\n<p>4 = 4 is true, so this ordered pair is on the line.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(-8, 0)\"></span></p>\n<p> <span data-math=\"0 = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( { - 8} \\right) + 4\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 = -4 + 4\"></span></p>\n<p>0 = 0 is true, so this ordered pair is on the line.</p>\n<p>Two points are all it takes to determine a line, so this is the correct equation for the line.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4\">y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 4</span>"
    }
